<title>SWEDEN: Handelsbanken 9 mo op profit rises 19 pct.</title>
<headline>Handelsbanken 9 mo op profit rises 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish commercial bank Handelsbanken reports for nine months to September 30.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  4,520 vs   3,794</p>
<p> Profit before credit losses	   5,827 vs   5,558</p>
<p> Interest receiveable		   29,622 vs  29,486</p>
<p> Leasing income				895 vs     773</p>
<p> Interest payable			 22,666 vs  22,870</p>
<p> Dividends received			  105 vs	56</p>
<p> Commissions receiveable		 2,303 vs   1,930</p>
<p> Commission payable			  330 vs     270</p>
<p> Net profit from fin ops		   906 vs     910</p>
<p> Other income				  186 vs     493</p>
<p> Total operating income		 11,021 vs  10,508</p>
<p> Personnel costs			   2,608 vs   2,547</p>
<p> Other costs				 1,655 vs   1,547</p>
<p> Depreciation				  931 vs     856</p>
<p> Total costs				 5,194 vs   4,950</p>
<p> Loan losses				 1,241 vs   1,770</p>
<p> Changes in value of property    CREDIT 66 vs	 6 CHARGE</p>
<p> Pension provision		  CREDIT 131 vs	27 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					   1,172 vs   1,070</p>
<p> Net profit				  3,479 vs   2,699</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of commercial bank is Svenska Handelsbanken. Analysts polled by Reuters forecast a nine-month profit after credit losses of 4.52 bln skr.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
